{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558989020,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf38506ffeNcdxLsVq4pRFDx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40d0e930014l57Ru9DGgxp56","sessionID":"ses_e2bf38506ffeNcdxLsVq4pRFDx","messageID":"msg_1d40d03b0001NArz6fraR0yqBp","type":"tool","id":"call_062bd19260c74fc29037244a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":60,"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs, lines 1-60\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Shipped Instruction Embed Engine\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // A repository that took the shipped instruction template keeps its own lines somewhere\n8: // the template does not know about: at the top of the file, inside a section somebody\n9: // edited, in the Claude copy a previous install left behind. Replacing the file with the\n10: // current template is therefore a deletion, and it is silent, because nothing in the\n11: // repository records which of its lines belonged to it.\n12: //\n13: // So this engine never writes what it has not first shown and hashed. Composition happens\n14: // in memory and produces one new document per target; the plan prints every target, the\n15: // diff, the new block, the byte budget and the survival ledger, and hashes the composed\n16: // bytes. The backup directory is named after that digest, so apply lands exactly where the\n17: // plan pointed and the plan is the artefact the yes is given against. It backs up every\n18: // path it will touch before the first byte, then writes only inside a fixed allowlist that\n19: // is checked in code rather than described in a document.\n20: //\n21: // After the write it proves the composition against the bytes now on disk: every line the\n22: // repository had, inside or outside the template, must still be there, and every line\n23: // outside the repository block must be one the template ships. A violation restores from\n24: // the backup automatically and ends the run as a failure. The proof is a pure function so\n25: // it can also be read and driven on its own, and it requires the old document's own lines\n26: // rather than the parts the segmenter produced: a proof built from those parts can require\n27: // only what the reader managed to place, and a line it placed nowhere goes unclaimed.\n28: //\n29: // The four carry groups, in order, are the shape a repository's own text keeps: the block\n30: // it already had, the sections that match no shipped section, the local lines of a section\n31: // somebody edited, and the unique lines of a runtime copy that is folded away. A section\n32: // whose body is a released one is replaced with no carry, because every line of it is a\n33: // line the template already ships.\n34: //\n35: // Usage: agents-md-embed.cjs <plan|apply|restore> [options]\n36: // Exit codes: 0 nothing to do or done, 1 the proof failed or the run was cancelled,\n37: //             2 a precondition failed or a path fell outside the allowlist\n38: \n39: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: // 1. IMPORTS\n41: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: \n43: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n44: const crypto = require('node:crypto');\n45: const fs = require('node:fs');\n46: const os = require('node:os');\n47: const path = require('node:path');\n48: \n49: const { buildReport } = require('./agents-md-check.cjs');\n50: const { classifyFile } = require('./release-update.cjs');\n51: const {\n52:   deliveryAnchorEnd,\n53:   findBlock,\n54:   segment,\n55:   sha256,\n56: } = require('./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs');\n57: \