{"type":"text","timestamp":1794559156335,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf38506ffeNcdxLsVq4pRFDx","part":{"id":"prt_1d40f9172002cVXEJRmwTYTeB1","sessionID":"ses_e2bf38506ffeNcdxLsVq4pRFDx","messageID":"msg_1d40f7c30001a32TmAHSZ4pLio","type":"text","text":"## Report\n\n**Task:** T005 — undo a write that throws mid-apply and exit 3 (`EMB`, `EMBT`).\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs` — added `a write that throws mid-apply restores the backup and exits 3`: `claude-only` fixture, `--create-router`, write hook throws `EACCES` on its second call, records `treeDigest(dir)`, expects exit 3, `restored:` / `backup:` / `undo:` / `STATUS=FAIL`, and an identical tree digest after.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs` — wrapped the write loop in `commandApply` in `try`/`catch`; the catch prints `ERROR: writing <path> failed: <message>`, calls `restoreFromBackup`, prints the `backup:` and `undo:` lines, prints `STATUS=FAIL` and returns 3. Added exit 3 to the header exit-code lines and to `USAGE`, with a comment on why a partial write needs its own exit.\n\n**Before state (test-first)**\nThe new case failed with the thrown `EACCES` from `commandApply` at the write hook, exactly as the task predicted.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs\nℹ tests 38\nℹ pass 38\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n```\n$ node specs/.../014-review-remediation/scratch/planning/probe-embed-write-fault.cjs\nbefore: CLAUDE.md\nmain returned 3\napply printed backup line: true, undo line: true, restored line: true\nafter: CLAUDE.md\n```\n\n**Not done**\n- Checkbox not ticked in `tasks.md`, per the brief.\n- No git state touched, no other file edited. `git status` for the two named files shows only those two as modified. The diff in `agents-md-embed.cjs` also carries another worker's pre-existing `restoreFromBackup` hash-check changes, which I left untouched.","time":{"start":1794559152498,"end":1794559156335}}}
